fields.description:
On the hub registration form, there are two text boxes that allow you to input a different email to use when receiving email alerts and expert tips:

* {{emailalertemail}}
* {{commnewsemail}}

These emails are sent to the hub and input into their own DB fields.

If an admin changes their mind and decides to toggle off the ‘use different email’, the hub is not made aware of this and will presumably continue to send emails to the stored email values.  This is because we send null values for these params and the hub skips them during its validation, leaving what was originally set.

We need to force a reset of the email values at the hub when this occurs.

Error: 

Default exception handler: Error writing to database Debug: ERROR: duplicate key value violates unique constraint "mdl_userenro_enruse_uix"



The error seems caused by [https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-73845|https://moodle.atlassian.net/browse/MDL-73845|smart-link]



For example, suppose a course has three database enrolment instances with IDs *100, 101, and 102*.

User *200* is currently enrolled through enrolment instances *101* and *102*, meaning the user enrolment records are (enrolid, userid):

* (101, 200)
* (102, 200)

There is no enrolment record for (100, 200).

When the script runs, it attempts to reassign the user’s enrolments to the lowest enrol ID (100). This means it tries to update:

* (101, 200) → (100, 200)
* (102, 200) → (100, 200)

However, this creates duplicate records for (100, 200), which violates the *unique constraint* on enrolments.

[https://github.com/moodle/moodle/blob/MOODLE_405_STABLE/enrol/database/db/upgrade.php#L55-L81|https://github.com/moodle/moodle/blob/MOODLE_405_STABLE/enrol/database/db/upgrade.php#L55-L81|smart-link] 



SQL Query to check if a site will be affected by the regression (No record mean 'not affected')

{{SELECT}}
{{       ue.id,}}
{{       e.courseid,}}
{{       ue.userid,}}
{{       ue.enrolid,}}
{{       keeper.id as target_enrol_id}}
{{FROM prefix_user_enrolments ue}}
{{JOIN prefix_enrol e ON ue.enrolid = e.id}}
{{JOIN (}}
{{    SELECT courseid, MIN(id) as id}}
{{    FROM prefix_enrol}}
{{    WHERE enrol = 'database'}}
{{    GROUP BY courseid}}
{{    HAVING COUNT() > 2}}
{{) keeper ON e.courseid = keeper.courseid}}
{{WHERE e.enrol = 'database'}}
{{  AND e.id != keeper.id}}
{{  AND NOT EXISTS (}}
{{      SELECT 1}}
{{      FROM prefix_user_enrolments ue2}}
{{      WHERE ue2.userid = ue.userid}}
{{        AND ue2.enrolid = keeper.id}}
{{  )}}
{{  AND ue.userid IN (}}
{{      SELECT ue3.userid}}
{{      FROM prefix_user_enrolments ue3}}
{{      JOIN prefix_enrol e3 ON ue3.enrolid = e3.id}}
{{      WHERE e3.courseid = e.courseid}}
{{        AND e3.enrol = 'database'}}
{{      GROUP BY ue3.userid}}
{{      HAVING COUNT() >= 2}}
{{  )}}
{{ORDER BY e.courseid, ue.userid, ue.enrolid;}}
